  "worked_solution": "We are asked to compute the expected number of students tutored per day. This is a classic application of the law of total expectation, which allows us to calculate an overall expected value by conditioning on a related variable — in this case, the high school the tutor is assigned to.\n\nLet $X$ be the number of students tutored in a day, and let $Y$ be the school to which the tutor is assigned.\n\n- $Y=A$ with probability $0.45,$ and $\\text{E}[X∣Y=A]=4.8.$\n\n- $Y=B$ with probability $0.55,$ and $\\text{E}[X∣Y=B]=6.2.$\n\nSo, we calculate our expected value as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =\\text{E}[X∣Y=A]\\cdot P(Y=A)+\\text{E}[X∣Y=B]\\cdot P(Y=B) \\\\  & =4.8\\cdot 0.45+6.2\\cdot 0.55 \\\\  & =2.16+3.41 \\\\  & =5.57\\end{aligned}\n$$",
